@startuml
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

package "Identity & Access Context" as IAC {
  [Login Screen (Vaadin)] as LoginUI
  [Spring Security Filter Chain] as Security
  [User (aggregate root)] as UserAgg
  database "users table" as UsersDb
}

package "Course Catalog Context" as CCC {
  [Course Catalog UI (Vaadin)] as CourseUI
  [Course (aggregate root)] as CourseAgg
  database "courses table" as CoursesDb
}

LoginUI --> Security : submits credentials
Security --> UserAgg : authenticate(username, password)
UserAgg --> UsersDb : reads/writes

Security ..> CourseUI : grants an\nauthenticated session\n<<upstream/downstream>>
CourseUI --> CourseAgg
CourseAgg --> CoursesDb

note bottom of IAC
  Owns everything about **who** can use the system:
  credentials, login/logout, and (later) roles and
  permissions. Doesn't know what a Course is.
end note

note bottom of CCC
  Owns the course catalog itself. Depends on
  Identity & Access only for "is there an
  authenticated user?" — a conformist relationship,
  via Spring Security's SecurityContext, not a
  direct dependency on the User aggregate.
end note

@enduml
